      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/VortixWx/status/1964838820215484843",
      "text": "#WxHistory |\n[🧵; 2feat.] #OTDwx: Typhoon Yagi ‘24 (Enteng) became the most significant typhoon of the year. Yagi was a very powerful typhoon in the South China Sea. At 165mph / 907mb, it’s the strongest typhoon in the SCS on record.\n\nYagi brought major flooding to the Philippines as it brushed by there. It then went to Hainan & directly went over the city of Haikou. It brought destructive wind gust well over 130mph (210kph). Yagi became the 2nd costliest typhoon in China’s history.\n\nThen Yagi slammed Vietnam, hitting as a high end C3, the strongest in the country’s history. Areas in N 🇻🇳, mainly around Hanoi was railed. Extreme storm surge, winds & flooding messed up much of that area. It became the country’s costliest disaster ever. Thailand & Myanmar faced a very high death toll from flooding.\n\nOverall, Yagi killed anywhere between 844 & 1,138. It dealt $14.7B in damages. Thankfully Yagi (and Enteng; Edring was its replacement) were retired. \n[1/2]",
